/// known-gap: interp skips a target whose score fails, so the decision silently does nothing
/// A decision formula that fails, or gives something other than a number,
/// stops the tick with an error that names the decision. Here a comparison
/// gives a bool, and a bool times a number is a type error.
<>F |
    side: 0
    hp: 10
    attack | decision against F by [
        (target >> side != self >> side) * (target >> hp)
    ]
    judge using attack
        > 0: hit(target)
    end
xx
act hit(f, t)
    say("hit")
xx
a <> F | side: 0
b <> F | side: 1
attempt
    tick()
rescue e
    say(:has("{e}", "R1220: decision-formula: decision `attack` of F"))
    say(:has("{e}", "got bool"))
xx
